# Resources

[(back to project README)](../README.md)

Resource YAML files in this directory define Databricks resources deployed by the bundle. Files here are auto-discovered via the `include: ./resources/*.yml` directive in `databricks.yml`.

## Ships with the scaffold

| File | Resources |
|------|-----------|
| `experiment.yml` | MLflow experiment with UC volume artifact location |
| `schemas.yml` | Unity Catalog schema for project resources |
| `volumes.yml` | UC volume for MLflow artifacts |

## Adding resources

Add a new `.yml` file to this directory following the DAB resource schema. Use the `databricks-bundles` skill (ai-dev-kit) for help authoring new resource types.

Common resource types:

- `jobs:` — scheduled workflows
- `apps:` — Databricks Apps
- `pipelines:` — Lakeflow / SDP pipelines
- `model_serving_endpoints:` — model serving
- `vector_search_endpoints:` / `vector_search_indexes:` — vector search

## Deployment semantics

- **Dev mode** prefixes resource names to isolate parallel developer deploys.
- **Production mode** uses exact names and rejects user-scoped workspace paths.
- Variables defined in `databricks.yml` are overridden per-target — see `${var.catalog}` and `${var.schema}`.

